  <section id="cp-references" aria-labelledby="cp-references-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="cp-references-title">7. Useful references</h2></div>
    </div>

    <p class="cp-lead">All six are books or book chapters that predate digital indexing, and none has a DOI of its own, so they are listed rather than given reference cards.</p>

    <ul class="cp-reflist">
      <li>Dicke, F. F. 1977. The most important corn insects. Chapter 9 in <em>Corn and Corn Improvement</em>, G. F. Sprague (ed.&#41;. American Society of Agronomy, Madison, Wisconsin.</li>
      <li>Larson, W. E., and J. J. Hanway. 1977. Corn production. Chapter 11 in <em>Corn and Corn Improvement</em>, G. F. Sprague (ed.&#41;. American Society of Agronomy, Madison, Wisconsin.</li>
      <li>Poehlman, J. M., and D. A. Sleper. 1995. Breeding corn (maize&#41;. In <em>Breeding Field Crops</em>, 4th edition. Iowa State University Press, Ames.</li>
      <li>Sheridan, W. F. (ed.&#41;. 1982. <em>Maize for Biological Research</em>. Plant Molecular Biology Association. ISBN 0-9608758-0-8. Chapter 3, &ldquo;Growing Maize for Genetic Purposes,&rdquo; by M. G. Neuffer, is the source of this protocol.</li>
      <li>Shurtleff, M. C. 1981. <em>A Compendium of Corn Diseases</em>. The American Phytopathological Society, St. Paul, Minnesota.</li>
      <li>Ullstrup, A. J. 1977. Diseases of corn. Chapter 8 in <em>Corn and Corn Improvement</em>, G. F. Sprague (ed.&#41;. American Society of Agronomy, Madison, Wisconsin.</li>
      <li>Wallace, H. A., and E. N. Bressman. 1937. <em>Corn and Corn Growing</em>. John Wiley and Sons, New York.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

